  "chronology_reasoning": "The complete official original yields sixteen operative units after removing nonoperative headings, combining roster labels with their governing membership/invitation language, and splitting the page-crossing 1-203/1-204 merge. The Council is indefinite: yearly reporting, quarterly meetings and developing/maintaining coordination mechanisms are ongoing duties, not own-term sunsets or report-triggered termination. EO12379 section 9 supplies an immediate August 17, 1982 revocation without delayed effectiveness or saving. No genuine earlier amendment to those general Council duties is located; inactivity is not treated as legal termination. Accordingly the fifteen nondependent units have supported first ends on August 17, 1982, establishing the last Council end, while the express Pension Policy Commission director seat needs a separate earlier-ending analysis. Full dependency originals EO12071 and EO12100 show a sunset and a ratified effective date, but OFR points to a statutory extension by Public Law96-14 whose actual terms are not held. The director-seat first_end remains null rather than importing either a 1979 sunset preceding this original or the 1982 cleanup. This concrete clause-level uncertainty keeps the whole lifecycle incomplete despite the supported terminal revocation. Machine-chain actor/date contamination is rejected and provisional no retained. No image verification, exhaustion or human review is claimed.",
