    "reason": "The full original and revoker contain no express saving, transfer of Council duties, or independent future command beyond the Council. Coordination, research, common facilities/data, evaluation, annual reporting, quarterly meetings, support and subcommittees are Council functions. The order does not itself create ERISA benefit entitlements or repeal the independent responsibilities of member agencies. Commission-on-Pension-Policy staff authority arises under separate EO 12071/12100, not as a surviving EO 12262 command. Earlier ending of that director membership remains a first-end gap, not evidence of a continuing Council residual. This finding is bounded to the held complete original, revoker, and dependency orders.",
    "source": {
      "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1982-08-19/pdf/FR-1982-08-19.pdf",
      "sha256": "5432431cc09039ad5672f86f17e1fb6dddf44075581197caa24cd70f1448da4a",
      "page_or_item": "47 FR 36099, PDF page 9, section 9; 47 FR 36100, PDF page 10, signature and complete ending",
      "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_12379.txt",
      "text_sha256": "c7c738d02047e0faabb73bdca7b9cbf5cb9953abb67a629f658cb125eb3f1613",
      "read_method": "complete held official extract; no image verification asserted",
      "official_fixity_record": "jobs/official-fixity/output/MATCHED_BY_SHA256.json",
      "official_fixity_result": "match",
      "quoted_parts": [
        "Sec. 9. Executive Order No. 12262, establishing an Interagency Employee  \nBenefit Council, is revoked.",
        "THE W H ITE HOUSE, \nA u g u s t 17, 1982."
      ]
    },
    "supporting_sources": [
      {
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-09/pdf/FR-1981-01-09.pdf",
        "sha256": "400087effcd187e70ba14828f1000d0d9134cc11fcbee52819886fe0abc12771",
        "page_or_item": "46 FR 2313-2314, PDF pages 9-10, sections 1-201 and 1-206 through 1-304",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_12262.txt",
        "text_sha256": "181058bc118fcb0feb604ee7c5b5fffafb0ddf5709b88e7d58bcb115769000ab",
        "read_method": "complete held official extract; no image verification asserted",
        "official_fixity_record": "jobs/official-fixity/output/MATCHED_BY_SHA256.json",
        "official_fixity_result": "match",
        "quoted_parts": [
          "1-201. The Council shall assist in interagency coordination of proposals \naffecting employee benefits under ERISA. It shall identify the potential eco­\nnomic consequences of those proposals for ERISA participants.",
          "1-206. The Council shall establish and m aintain a m echanism  to evaluate the \neffectiveness of the overall ER ISA  program.\n1-207. The Council shall submit annually to the President a summary report of \nsignificant ERISA -related achievem ents of the m em ber agencies.",
          "1-301. The Council shall m eet at le ast once each quarter.\n1-302. Each m em ber agency with respect to m atters within the jurisdiction of \nthe agency shall cooperate w ith and assist the Council in performing its \nfunctions.\n1-303. The Secretary  of Labor shall be responsible for providing the Council \nwith such adm inistrative services and support as may be necessary.\n1-304. The Council may establish such working groups or subcommittees as \nmay be appropriate for the conduct of the Council’s functions."
        ]
